# [AUDIT FIX] Replaced `*.env` glob with explicit `.env` + negation of .env.example.
# The glob `*.env` matched both `.env` AND `.env.example`, meaning the example
# template file (which SHOULD be committed to source control) could be silently
# excluded by some git client implementations. The explicit pattern below is
# unambiguous: ignore only the real secrets file, never the example. (audit: .gitignore L1)
.env
!.env.example

*/__pycache__
__pycache__/
venv/
.venv/

# Local data files used during development (not needed in source control)
Spond/
spondRE
upcoming
login
